# taf.ul.gnb.bip.collection

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/taf-ul-gnb-bip-collection/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.gnb.bip.collection/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.gnb.bip.collection/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.gnb.bip.collection/-/badges/release.svg)][3]


taf.ul.gnb.bip.collection library

This library provides a simple robot interface for bip collection:

Start bip Trace
Stop Bip trace

The taf admin libraries are used to determine the hw and version.
Depending on the setup the port mirroring is executed and the trace
collection is started and stopped and finally the collected pcaps are
stored into a given directory.

Until the introduction of CB008729, different ways of bip collection are
existing in robotws, with this new feature, the collection should get
harmonized from bts side. This library also support this new way of
bip collection.


## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`python_requires` option in [setup.py](setup.py).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].


